      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discovery should be able to succeed even if there is no A or AAAA record known yet\n\nThis seems to be the fundamental difference between service found and resolved; mdns responders are not required to reply with the A and AAAA record for a SVC query AFAIK; see rfc6763 12.1 and 12.2, including the records in the \"additional records\" section is a SHOULD, not a requirement.\n\nSo at least here there should be a difference between service found and resolved, where found doesn\u0027t require the response to be \"complete\".\n\nAlso we should (probably separately) send additional queries for the other records if the response is not complete (only has PTR records as replies for example). And have tests for that; maybe file a bug",
